{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgemixMH9GRAKfZXXryEC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ruled F1 **FIX** and committed the verdict as 7a6683edb (`docs/reviews/wi-978/018-ADJUDICATE-d3a3531.md`). The commit ends with `WI: WI-978` and `Loop-Session: 20261102T035202Z-8dc8b4` in the same trailer block.\n\n- **The defect is real.** The landing check collects the ids a landing adds over the lane's merge base, and returns before looking at retirement records if there are none. Say SR-003 was already live at the base, the lane retires it with `retire.py`, then authors a different SR-003. That id is never \"added\", so the check passes, even with the retirement record in the tree. Called directly, the same id treated as added is refused, naming its record. Nothing in the retirement checks flags a live row that also has a retirement record.\n- **In scope under §6.** §6 counts content that agents write into the repo. The steps are the kit's own routes, and the slip is a natural one for a model author asked to replace a row: retire it, then write \"the replacement\" under the same id. It's less likely than sitting 008's in-range case, because nothing in the brief points at the number. But it's the same misuse, and the record that would refuse it is already there.\n- **Why FIX and not SUCCESSOR:** SR-174, as this lane widened it, promises a freed identity is never re-issued. A fail-open of that promise can't be deferred to a successor, and the fix is cheap.\n- **The fix:**\n  - **The refusal:** at the landing check both routes share, refuse a live id that a retirement record names, at least where the landing adds the record or changes the row. Limiting it that way keeps an old pair already on trunk from blocking unrelated landings.\n  - **The kept refusals:** the existing refusals stay.\n  - **The regression:** add a regression through both routes that fails on today's code.\n  - **The spine:** amend LLR-363 and TC-402 through their own authority.\n\nThe verdict discloses that this gap is partly mine. My sitting-008 ruling worded the refusal as applying to \"an added id\", and the lane built exactly that. I also approved LLR-363 and TC-402 with that wording at sitting 013, so the amendment will need another sitting.\n\nThe commit hooks passed, but again reported that the `format` check didn't run (ruff isn't installed). I committed only the verdict, so `018-ADJUDICATE-d3a3531.md.requested` is still untracked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":576172,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":589},"output_tokens":688,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f031c6a5-ecf0-490f-9890-c7a8a87f92fc","uuid":"c33a3c7d-d144-4908-8652-1a82ac42512b","timestamp":"2026-11-02T20:58:30.214Z","request_id":"req_011Cgemix4RG3XdhVpPpZDxa"}
